9. AI Verification
We also learned an important engineering habit:

Never accept an AI-generated answer simply because it sounds confident. Verify the claim by testing it against the actual Python system.

This develops critical thinking, debugging, and technical judgment.


🏆 Final Learning
This topic taught us how to create, access, slice, modify, add, remove, and reorder data using Python lists. Most importantly, we learned that lists are mutable “parts bins,” unlike immutable strings, and that reliable programmers verify AI-generated claims through actual testing.

